# Secret group `postgres`: The deploy/docker-compose.yml `postgres` container's own init-time superuser and database.
# Loaded by: semprec-backup.service (and `docker compose --env-file` in provision.sh).
#
# Ownership and mode are load-bearing: `root:root 0600`. systemd reads EnvironmentFile= as root
# before dropping privileges. provision.sh installs this template to
# /opt/semprec/shared/env/postgres.env only when that file does not exist, so an operator's values are
# never overwritten by a rerun, and it never prints a value. A key belongs to exactly one group
# (docs/adr/2026-10-03-per-service-secret-groups.md); this file is excluded from restic backups.

# POSTGRES_USER / POSTGRES_PASSWORD / POSTGRES_DB: the deploy/docker-compose.yml `postgres`
# container's own init-time superuser and database — used once, by the operator, to connect and
# create the two least-privilege roles (see data-role.env and side-role.env) (docs/operations/database-roles.md). No application
# process ever authenticates as this user.
POSTGRES_USER=
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
POSTGRES_DB=semprec
